305574816, 41445410045, …\\n—\\n12/20 every week\\n\\n\\n\\nThe same 8 cases fail every week:\\n\\nHumanEval/1, 3, 6, 7, 11, 17, 19: answer contains no Python code\\nHumanEval/4: the emitted program fails check(mean_absolute_deviation) with a traceback\\n\\nReproduction (no build needed)\\nUsing the released static CLI v0.355.34 (formal-ai-cli-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl):\\nformal-ai benchmark run --suite humaneval --offset 3 --slice 1 --online --repository-root \\\"$PWD\\\"\\n# suite=humaneval passed=0 failed=1 total=1\\n# FAIL HumanEval/3 answer contains no Python code\\nThe same command with --offset 4 gives FAIL HumanEval/4 answer contains no Python code (locally the solver refuses; the CI run emitted a wrong program).\\nThe answer text shows why. Run formal-ai chat --thinking --prompt \\\"&lt;benchmark prompt for HumanEval/3&gt;\\\"; the benchmark prompt is Complete this Python function. Reply with the full implementation in a ```python code block. followed by the below_zero stub:\\nRoute to the write program skill gap handler.\\nI cannot write this program: no synthesis route reaches task \\\"below_zero\\\" in language \\\"python\\\".\\nI decomposed the request and tried every synthesis route I have, in order — catalog, blueprint_recipes, coding_oracle, seed_idiom_composer — and none of them derives it.\\n\\nSo none of the synthesis routes derives the task any more, and the honest skill-gap answer (#699) is returned.\\nBisect bounds\\nThe regression lands between efb6ddb (v0.351.0, 20/20) and d209aac (v0.352.1, 12/20). The first-parent merges in that window are #1139 (worktree-issue-1138), #1140, #1141, #1144, #1146, #1148, #1152 and #1150.\\nWithin #1139, the coding-synthesis rewrite is the strongest candidate:\\n\\n9c31b05 \\\"land the codex continuation waves in one bulk state\\\" deletes src/coding/structural_composition.rs (632 lines). It replaces src/coding/composition.rs and src/coding/concept_discovery.rs with rust/src/coding/composition_search/*, program_ir* and ir_lowering/*.\\nc2d982a, 9b3b641, fd88a17 and 4ab9e3e (2026-09-17 to 09-18) are follow-ups to the composition search.\\nbcf1e8e and e8533a5 (2026-09-20/21) change data/seed/meanings-coding-structure.lino, which is 518 lines smaller net across the window.\\n\\nOnly 300–400 MB desktop bundles are published for v0.351.0 and v0.352.1, so I did not bisect with binaries. Building each candidate commit would pin the exact commit.\\nExpected\\nHumanEval slice 20 passes ≥ 20/20 again, through derivation rather than recited templates, so the ratchet holds. Alternatively, if a deliberate design change caused the drop, the ledger should record that decision explicitly instead of the workflow failing silently every week.Activitykonardadded a commit that references this issue on Nov 15, 2026docs(experiments): keep the humaneval regression report filed as #1574 (...7b8fc7cSign up for free to join this conversation on GitHub. Already have an account? Sign in to commentMetadataMetadataAssigneesNo one assignedLabelsNo labelsNo labelsTypeNo typeProjectsNo projectsMilestoneNo milestoneRelationshipsNone yetDevelopmentNo branches or pull requestsIssue actionsOpen in GitHub Copilot app\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n\\n\\n\\n    \\n  \\n\\n  \\n\\n  \\n            \\n  Footer\\n\\n  \\n\\n\\n  \\n    \\n      \\n        \\n    \\n\\n\\n      \\n        &copy; 2026 GitHub,&nbsp;Inc.\\n      \\n    \\n\\n    \\n      Footer navigation\\n\\n      \\n\\n\\n          \\n            Terms\\n          \\n\\n          \\n            Privacy\\n          \\n\\n\\n            \\n              Security\\n            \\n\\n            \\n              Status\\n            \\n\\n          \\n            Community\\n          \\n\\n          \\n            Docs\\n          \\n\\n          \\n            Contact\\n          \\n\\n          \\n\\n  \\n    \\n      Manage cookies\\n    \\n  \\n\\n\\n  \\n    \\n      \\n        Do not share my personal information\\n      \\n    \\n  \\n\\n      \\n    \\n  \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n    \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n    \\n    \\n\\n    \\n      \\n    \\n\\n    \\n    You can’t perform that action at this time.\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"Let me take the next step to handle that for you.\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call_2cc8b73911287f64\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"glob\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"**/external-benchmarks.yml\\\"}\"}}]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call_2cc8b73911287f64\",\"content\":\"/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1794762838837/.github/workflows/external-benchmarks.yml\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"Let me open /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1794762838837/.github/workflows/external-benchmarks.yml and read what it says.\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call_1e785f4e99493a48\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"read\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1794762838837/.github/workflows/external-benchmarks.yml\\\"}\"}}]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call_1e785f4e99493a48\",\"content\":\"<file>\\n00001| # Scheduled external benchmark harness (issue #698).\\n00002| #\\n00003| # Runs a bounded slice of every real upstream suite, records the honest\\n00004| # `passed/total` score in `data/benchmarks/external-results.lino`, verifies the\\n00005| # monotonic per-suite ratchet, and commits the refreshed ledger. A suite that\\n00006| # cannot run is recorded as `benchmark_unavailable` with its reason instead of\\n00007| # being replaced by a repository-local proxy.\\n00008| name: External Benchmarks\\n00009| \\n00010| on:\\n00011|   pull_request:\\n00012|     paths-ignore:\\n00013|       - \\\"docs/**\\\"\\n00014|       - \\\"*.md\\\"\\n00015|       - \\\"**/README.md\\\"\\n00016|       - \\\"**/CHANGELOG.md\\\"\\n00017|       - \\\"changelog.d/**\\\"\\n00018|     # Issue #1187 R4: an isolated e2e/<purpose>/<run>/<name> pull request\\n00019|     # never triggers this repository's own pipeline.\\n00020|     branches-ignore: ['e2e/**']\\n00021|   schedule:\\n00022|     # Weekly, Monday 04:17 UTC. Off the hour so the run does not queue behind\\n00023|     # the GitHub-wide top-of-hour cron burst.\\n00024|     - cron: '17 4 * * 1'\\n00025|   workflow_dispatch:\\n00026|     inputs:\\n00027|       slice:\\n00028|         description: 'Upstream cases per core suite (first N in upstream order)'\\n00029|         required: false\\n00030|         type: string\\n00031|         default: '20'\\n00032|       swebench_slice:\\n00033|         description: 'SWE-bench cases (container-heavy; first N in upstream order)'\\n00034|         required: false\\n00035|         type: string\\n00036|         default: '23'\\n00037|       suite:\\n00038|         description: 'Suite id, or `all` for every recorded suite'\\n00039|         required: false\\n00040|         type: string\\n00041|         default: 'all'\\n00042|       commit:\\n00043|         description: 'Commit the refreshed ledger back to the branch'\\n00044|         required: false\\n00045|         type: boolean\\n00046|         default: true\\n00047|       shard_size:\\n00048|         description: 'Split one suite (not `all`) into concurrent shards of this many cases; empty runs it in one job. Shards never commit.'\\n00049|         required: false\\n00050|         type: string\\n00051|         default: ''\\n00052| \\n00053| permissions:\\n00054|   contents: read\\n00055| \\n00056| env:\\n00057|   CARGO_NET_RETRY: '10'\\n00058|   CARGO_TERM_COLOR: always\\n00059| \\n00060| jobs:\\n00061|   pr-check-profile:\\n00062|     if: (github.event_name == 'pull_request' || (github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch' && github.ref != 'refs/heads/main'))\\n00063|     uses: ./.github/workflows/pull-request-check-profile.yml\\n00064|   # === RATCHET - every PR compares its ledger with the actual base revision ===\\n00065|   ratchet:\\n00066|     if: ${{ (github.event_name != 'pull_request' && github.event_name != 'pull_request_target' && (github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' || github.event_name == 'release' || (github.event_name == 'workflow_run' && github.event.workflow_run.head_branch == 'main'))) && (true) }}\\n00067|     name: Verify monotonic ledger\\n00068|     concurrency:\\n00069|       group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}-ratchet\\n00070|       cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' }}\\n00071|     runs-on: ubuntu-latest\\n00072|     timeout-minutes: 15\\n00073|     steps:\\n00074|       - uses: actions/checkout@v7\\n00075|         with:\\n00076|           persist-credentials: false\\n00077|           fetch-depth: 0\\n00078| \\n00079|       - name: Setup Rust\\n00080|         uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable\\n00081| \\n00082|       - name: Compare with pull-request base\\n00083|         if: github.event_name == 'pull_request'\\n00084|         run: |\\n00085|           set -euo pipefail\\n00086|           cargo run --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml --locked --bin formal-ai -- benchmark ratchet \\\\\\n00087|             --base-ref \\\"origin/${GITHUB_BASE_REF}\\\"\\n00088| \\n00089|       - name: Verify scheduled branch ledger\\n00090|         if: github.event_name != 'pull_request'\\n00091|         run: |\\n00092|           set -euo pipefail\\n00093|           cargo run --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml --locked --bin formal-ai -- benchmark ratchet\\n00094| \\n00095|   # === EXTERNAL BENCHMARKS - run upstream suites and publish honest scores ===\\n00096|   external-benchmarks:\\n00097|     name: Run upstream suites\\n00098|     concurrency:\\n00099|       group: formal-ai-repository-writes\\n00100|       queue: max\\n00101|     if: github.event_name != 'pull_request' && !inputs.shard_size && (github.event_name != 'pull_request' && github.event_name != 'pull_request_target' && (github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' || github.event_name == 'release' || (github.event_name == 'workflow_run' && github.event.workflow_run.head_branch == 'main')))\\n00102|     runs-on: ubuntu-latest\\n00103|     timeout-minutes: 90\\n00104|     permissions:\\n00105|       contents: write\\n00106|     steps:\\n00107|       # One of the four checkouts in this repository that keep their\\n00108|       # credential (issue #1079); every other one sets\\n00109|       # `persist-credentials: fal…his\\n00110|       # job pushes through `scripts/push-to-shared-branch.sh` to record the\\n00111|       # scheduled upstream results, and that push authenticates with exactly the\\n00112|       # credential `persist-credentials: fal…ady\\n00113|       # narrowed to `github.event_name != 'pull_request'`, so the credential is\\n00114|       # never persisted on a fork's pull request.\\n00115|       - uses: actions/checkout@v7\\n00116|         with:\\n00117|           fetch-depth: 0\\n00118| \\n00119|       - name: Setup Rust\\n00120|         uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable\\n00121| \\n00122|       - uses: ./.github/actions/cache-cargo-registry\\n00123| \\n00124|       - name: Setup Python\\n00125|         # HumanEval/MBPP execute upstream tests. SWE-bench applies candidate\\n00126|         # patches in its official Docker evaluator.\\n00127|         uses: actions/setup-python@v7\\n00128|         with:\\n00129|           python-version: '3.12'\\n00130| \\n00131|       # Do not preinstall SWE-bench here. The grader recovers the pinned\\n00132|       # official harness through the same prerequisite pipeline users exercise,\\n00133|       # and records whether the evaluator was reached (issue #1138 plan 06).\\n00134| \\n00135|       # Reused across every workflow that only needs to *run* the binary: the\\n00136|       # cache key is the content of the sources it is built from, so a push that\\n00137|       # changed neither pays nothing (issue #1107).\\n00138|       - uses: ./.github/actions/formal-ai-binary\\n00139| \\n00140|       - name: Run the bounded upstream slice\\n00141|         env:\\n00142|           BENCHMARK_SLICE: ${{ inputs.slice || '20' }}\\n00143|           SWE_BENCH_SLICE: ${{ inputs.swebench_slice || '23' }}\\n00144|           BENCHMARK_SUITE: ${{ inputs.suite || 'all' }}\\n00145|         run: |\\n00146|           set -euo pipefail\\n00147|           mkdir -p ci-logs\\n00148|           # Issue #1569: one failing suite must not hide the others. Under\\n00149|           # `set -e` the first failure ended the loop: every weekly run from\\n00150|           # 2026-10-26 to 2026-11-02 stopped after humaneval (12/20), so the\\n00151|           # other nine suites produced no result at all. Every selected suite\\n00152|           # runs now, each failure is named, and the step still fails.\\n00153|           failed=''\\n00154|           run_suite() {\\n00155|             ./rust/target/release/formal-ai benchmark run \\\\\\n00156|               --suite \\\"$1\\\" \\\\\\n00157|               --slice \\\"$2\\\" \\\\\\n00158|               --online \\\\\\n00159|               --allow-install \\\\\\n00160|               --append \\\\\\n00161|               --learning-report \\\"target/formal-ai-benchmarks/learning/$1.lino\\\" \\\\\\n00162|               --frontier-record data/meta/learning-frontier-upstream-benchmarks.lino || {\\n00163|               echo \\\"::error title=External benchmark $1 failed::formal-ai benchmark run --suite $1 exited non-zero; the remaining suites still ran\\\"\\n00164|               failed=\\\"${failed} $1\\\"\\n00165|             }\\n00166|           }\\n00167|           status=0\\n00168|           {\\n00169|             if [[ \\\"${BENCHMARK_SUITE}\\\" == 'all' ]]; then\\n00170|               for suite in humaneval mbpp gsm8k math object_counting coedit egg_math editeval; do\\n00171|                 run_suite \\\"${suite}\\\" \\\"${BENCHMARK_SLICE}\\\"\\n00172|               done\\n00173|               run_suite ascent_transitive_closure 5\\n00174|               run_suite swebench_lite \\\"${SWE_BENCH_SLICE}\\\"\\n00175|             elif [[ \\\"${BENCHMARK_SUITE}\\\" == 'swebench_lite' ]]; then\\n00176|               run_suite \\\"${BENCHMARK_SUITE}\\\" \\\"${SWE_BENCH_SLICE}\\\"\\n00177|             elif [[ \\\"${BENCHMARK_SUITE}\\\" == 'ascent_transitive_closure' ]]; then\\n00178|               run_suite \\\"${BENCHMARK_SUITE}\\\" 5\\n00179|             else\\n00180|               run_suite \\\"${BENCHMARK_SUITE}\\\" \\\"${BENCHMARK_SLICE}\\\"\\n00181|             fi\\n00182|             if [[ -n \\\"${failed}\\\" ]]; then\\n00183|               echo \\\"failed suites:${failed}\\\"\\n00184|               exit 1\\n00185|             fi\\n00186|           } 2>&1 | tee ci-logs/external-benchmarks.log || status=$?\\n00187|           grep -E '^suite=' ci-logs/external-benchmarks.log >> \\\"${GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY}\\\"\\n00188|           exit \\\"${status}\\\"\\n00189| \\n00190|       - name: Verify the monotonic ratchet\\n00191|         run: |\\n00192|           set -euo pipefail\\n00193|           ./rust/target/release/formal-ai benchmark ratchet\\n00194| \\n00195|       - name: Upload run log\\n00196|         if: always()\\n00197|         uses: actions/upload-artifact@v7\\n00198|         with:\\n00199|           name: external-benchmarks-log\\n00200|           path: |\\n00201|             ci-logs/external-benchmarks.log\\n00202|             target/formal-ai-benchmarks/learning/*.lino\\n00203|           if-no-files-found: warn\\n00204| \\n00205|       # This push does not trigger a pipeline run, and that is documented\\n00206|       # behaviour rather than a fault here (issue #1081, D4):\\n00207|       #\\n00208|       #   \\\"When you use the repository's GITHUB_TOKEN to perform tasks, events\\n00209|       #    triggered by the GITHUB_TOKEN [...] will not create a new workflow\\n00210|       #    run. This prevents you from accidentally creating recursive workflow\\n00211|       #    runs.\\\"\\n00212|       #   https://docs.github.com/en/actions/security-for-github-actions/security-guides/automatic-token-authentication\\n00213|       #\\n00214|       # So the tree at the tip of the default branch after this step has never\\n00215|       # been validated, and -- because there is no run at all, rather than a\\n00216|       # failed one -- the branch page keeps showing the previous commit's green.\\n00217|       # Measured on 2026-09-07: `dda02efb` received zero push-triggered runs\\n00218|       # while `6039c4d9` under it received the full fan-out.\\n00219|       #\\n00220|       # Neither available remedy is safe. A personal access token would restore\\n00221|       # the runs and restore the recursion the rule exists to prevent, and\\n00222|       # `release.yml`'s `workflow_dispatch` means \\\"publish a release\\\" (it\\n00223|       # requires `release_mode` and `bump_type`, and its `detect-changes` job is\\n00224|       # skipped on that event), not \\\"validate this commit\\\". What is fixed is the\\n00225|       # invisibility: `scripts/check-head-pipeline-coverage.rs` runs weekly from\\n00226|       # `.github/workflows/job-headroom.yml` and says out loud when the tip has\\n00227|       # no run and how many commits back the last validated tree is.\\n00228|       - name: Commit the refreshed ledger\\n00229|         if: github.event_name == 'schedule' || inputs.commit\\n00230|         run: |\\n00231|           set -euo pipefail\\n00232|           if git diff --quiet -- data/benchmarks/external-results.lino 'data/meta/learning-frontier-upstream-benchmarks*.lino'; then\\n00233|             echo 'ledger unchanged; nothing to commit'\\n00234|             exit 0\\n00235|           fi\\n00236|           git config user.name 'github-actions[bot]'\\n00237|           git config user.email '41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com'\\n00238|           git add data/benchmarks/external-results.lino 'data/meta/learning-frontier-upstream-benchmarks*.lino'\\n00239|           git commit -m 'chore(benchmarks): record scheduled upstream results and the failure frontier (#698, #1085)'\\n00240|           # Issue #1081 (D13). `concurrency: formal-ai-repository-writes` above\\n00241|           # orders this job against the release writers; it does not rebase it.\\n00242|           # This job is checked out at the commit its cron fired on, so a\\n00243|           # release that lands while it waits in the queue leaves it behind the\\n00244|           # branch and its push is rejected non-fast-forward -- a red scheduled\\n00245|           # run with nothing wrong in it, and a ledger update lost. The helper\\n00246|           # rebases and retries, and refuses to retry a rejection a rebase\\n00247|           # cannot fix.\\n00248|           bash scripts/push-to-shared-branch.sh origin \\\"${GITHUB_REF_NAME}\\\"\\n00249| \\n00250|   # === SHARDED MEASUREMENT - one suite split into concurrent windows ===\\n00251|   #\\n00252|   # A full HumanEval slice spends about 55 seconds per case in the solver\\n00253|   # (run 37594798452: 89 cases in 81 minutes, one case taking 164 seconds), so\\n00254|   # 164 cases cannot finish inside one job cap -- and grading happens after the\\n00255|   # last case, so a cancelled run reports nothing at all. Each shard here runs\\n00256|   # `--offset`/`--slice` windows of the same suite, grades its own window, and\\n00257|   # the total job adds the windows up. Shards read only; their combined count\\n00258|   # is recorded in the ledger by a reviewed commit, never by one shard.\\n00259|   shard-plan:\\n00260|     name: Plan upstream shards\\n00261|     concurrency:\\n00262|       group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}-${{ inputs.suite }}-shard-plan\\n00263|       cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' }}\\n00264|     if: ${{ (github.event_name != 'pull_request' && github.event_name != 'pull_request_target' && (github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' || github.event_name == 'release' || (github.event_name == 'workflow_run' && github.event.workflow_run.head_branch == 'main'))) && (github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch' && inputs.shard_size) }}\\n00265|     runs-on: ubuntu-latest\\n00266|     timeout-minutes: 30\\n00267|     outputs:\\n00268|       windows: ${{ steps.plan.outputs.windows }}\\n00269|     steps:\\n00270|       - uses: actions/checkout@v7\\n00271|         with:\\n00272|           persist-credentials: false\\n00273| \\n00274|       - name: Plan the windows\\n00275|         id: plan\\n00276|         env:\\n00277|           SUITE: ${{ inputs.suite }}\\n00278|           SLICE: ${{ inputs.slice }}\\n00279|           SHARD_SIZE: ${{ inputs.shard_size }}\\n00280|         run: |\\n00281|           set -euo pipefail\\n00282|           if [[ \\\"${SUITE}\\\" == 'all' ]]; then\\n00283|             echo '::error::shard_size splits one suite; dispatch it with a suite id, not all' >&2\\n00284|             exit 1\\n00285|           fi\\n00286|           windows=\\\"$(jq -cn --argjson total \\\"${SLICE}\\\" --argjson size \\\"${SHARD_SIZE}\\\" \\\\\\n00287|             '[range(0; $total; $size) | {offset: ., slice: ([$size, $total - .] | min)}]')\\\"\\n00288|           echo \\\"windows=${windows}\\\" >> \\\"${GITHUB_OUTPUT}\\\"\\n00289|           echo \\\"${windows}\\\"\\n00290| \\n00291|       - name: Setup Rust\\n00292|         uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable\\n00293| \\n00294|       - uses: ./.github/actions/cache-cargo-registry\\n00295| \\n00296|       # Built once here so every shard restores the same cached binary instead\\n00297|       # of each compiling it.\\n00298|       - uses: ./.github/actions/formal-ai-binary\\n00299| \\n00300|   upstream-shard:\\n00301|     if: ${{ (github.event_name != 'pull_request' && github.event_name != 'pull_request_target' && (github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' || github.event_name == 'release' || (github.event_name == 'workflow_run' && github.event.workflow_run.head_branch == 'main'))) }}\\n00302|     name: Upstream shard ${{ matrix.window.offset }}\\n00303|     concurrency:\\n00304|       group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}-${{ inputs.suite }}-shard-${{ matrix.window.offset }}\\n00305|       cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' }}\\n00306|     needs: shard-plan\\n00307|     runs-on: ubuntu-latest\\n00308|     timeout-minutes: 45\\n00309|     strategy:\\n00310|       fail-fast: false\\n00311|       matrix:\\n00312|         window: ${{ fromJSON(needs.shard-plan.outputs.windows) }}\\n00313|     steps:\\n00314|       - uses: actions/checkout@v7\\n00315|         with:\\n00316|           persist-credentials: false\\n00317| \\n00318|       - name: Setup Rust\\n00319|         uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable\\n00320| \\n00321|       - uses: ./.github/actions/cache-cargo-registry\\n00322| \\n00323|       - name: Setup Python\\n00324|         uses: actions/setup-python@v7\\n00325|         with:\\n00326|           python-version: '3.12'\\n00327| \\n00328|       - uses: ./.github/actions/formal-ai-binary\\n00329| \\n00330|       - name: Run the window\\n00331|         env:\\n00332|           SUITE: ${{ inputs.suite }}\\n00333|           OFFSET: ${{ matrix.window.offset }}\\n00334|           WINDOW: ${{ matrix.window.slice }}\\n00335|         run: |\\n00336|           set -euo pipefail\\n00337|           mkdir -p ci-logs\\n00338|           ./rust/target/release/formal-ai benchmark run \\\\\\n00339|             --suite \\\"${SUITE}\\\" \\\\\\n00340|             --offset \\\"${OFFSET}\\\" \\\\\\n00341|             --slice \\\"${WINDOW}\\\" \\\\\\n00342|             --online \\\\\\n00343|             --allow-install 2>&1 | tee \\\"ci-logs/shard-${OFFSET}.log\\\"\\n00344|           grep -E '^(shard )?suite=' \\\"ci-logs/shard-${OFFSET}.log\\\" >> \\\"${GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY}\\\"\\n00345| \\n00346|       - name: Upload shard log\\n00347|         if: always()\\n00348|         uses: actions/upload-artifact@v7\\n00349|         with:\\n00350|           name: external-benchmarks-shard-${{ matrix.window.offset }}\\n00351|           path: ci-logs/shard-*.log\\n00352|           if-no-files-found: warn\\n00353| \\n00354|   shard-total:\\n00355|     name: Total of